    "turn_text": "Well, that's true. It's good to be with you, Mike. Thanks for having me. Yeah, the view was frankly ridiculous fun. Look, it is a place where there's not a whole lot of common sense to put it mildly. But the reason I went on was simple, which is that I think conservatives, we spend too much time preaching to the choir, too much time talking to the same 2.6 million people who watch Fox News every night. And God loved the choir. The choir needs love. But we've got to reach much broader than that. We've got to be talking to young people. We've got to be talking to Hispanics and African Americans. We've got to be talking to suburban moms who are very much paying the price for the disastrous policies coming from Washington and who are being lied to every day by the corporate media. And so I went on because the folks who watch the view are used to getting one-sided political propaganda from the hosts. And I wanted them to see another side. The clip you played opened this up where Whoopi says, well, our side doesn't storm. My response was exactly what you said right after that, which is I said, I seem to remember an entire year of Antifa",
